                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex I]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summary of United States Initial Post-Defeat Policy
                        Relating to Japan</hi>
                </head>
                <p>[Here follows text as printed in annex to SWNCC 150, June 11, <ref
                        target="#pg549">page 549</ref>, except for revision of paragraph II as
                    follows:]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II. <hi rendition="#italic">Unconditional Surrender or Total
                        Defeat</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Immediately upon the unconditional surrender or total defeat of Japan, the
                    supreme allied commander will exercise supreme authority over the domestic and
                    foreign affairs of the Japanese Empire. Simultaneously, the powers of the
                    Emperor and the powers and functions of all instrumentalities which participate
                    in the formulation or consideration of national policies shall be assumed by the
                    military government.</p>
            </div>
